node_modules/
target/

/lib/

# Printing a tree as raw text writes a temporary artifact into the tree, and a debugging session
# leaves one behind per run — 149 accumulated at the repo root during the M1 spike before anyone
# noticed, at ~197 KB each. They are unreferenced by any code and are not the grammar: the grammar
# this plugin loads is the vendored `src/parser/tree-sitter-motoko.wasm`, which is committed and
# must stay that way. Scoped to the root so it cannot swallow a real artifact under `src/`.
/*.wasm

# Untracked scratch space (mirrors .prettierignore). Neither is committed, so neither should show
# up as noise in `git status` while the M1/M2 specs are being written.
/.probe/

# Harness output. Every run rewrites these, so committing them would dirty the tree on each
# invocation and make a real source change indistinguishable from a re-run; the workflow uploads
# RESULTS.md as a build artifact, which is where a run's numbers are read from.
#
# `tools/validate-moc2/RESULTS.md` is the exception and IS committed: it is the M3 release-notes
# artifact the plan asks for, so it is written by hand from a run rather than rewritten by one.
/tools/corpus/report.json
/tools/corpus/RESULTS.md
/tools/corpus/CHURN.md
/tools/validate-moc2/divergences.json
